<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</title>
<headline>Argentine monthly grain/oilseed shipments.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Secretariat April grain shipment figures (tonnes), followed by</p>
<p>January-March totals (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
<p> Wheat	753,471   (348,874)    5,857,077  (2,161,347)</p>
<p> Maize    2,429,281 (1,278,771)    4,132,970  (1,994,026)</p>
<p> Sorghum    167,110     83,713	 248,422    (115,785)</p>
<p> Barley	19,870	(nil)	 160,219	(6,888)</p>
<p> Soybeans   186,441   (189,447)	187,409    (291,743)</p>
<p> Sunseed	5,706    (94,641)	  7,396    (488,883)</p>
<p> Others	 4,106    (15,149)	  9,213     (55,762)</p>
<p>Principal destinations in April were as follows (tonnes):</p>
<p>WHEAT: Brazil 394,837; Peru 65,204; Jordan 62,498; Nigeria 40,279</p>
<p>MAIZE: Egypt 316,695; South Korea 298,765; Malaysia 251,996; Iran 173,566; Indonesia 160,942</p>
<p>((-- Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655))</p>
